A||N||3||Cozmo||Hidden outside door handles?||||5||
Z||000000||Cozmo||09-24-2001||07:54 PM||||An old street rodder trick is to shave the outside door handles off and install a solenoid operated door release mechanisim (either remote controlled or "kick the rocker panel type).<BR>On the Fiero doors, you could glue a couple of trim strips together and fill in the finger depression... Voila! no outside door handles!<BR>As a backup in case the electric stuff dies you could put in a cable release like the hood has...<BR>I never did like the way the door handles and finger holes break up the character lines of the car....<P>BobC||||reg||5
Z||000001||8Ball||09-24-2001||08:11 PM||||I was actually just thinking about that today. I had to put BOTH my cars, The hyundai (daily driver) and the Fiero (future daily driver) in the shop to be worked on. Well they guy who owns the place is a friend and is letting me work off my debt for the repairs as I am poor  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> atm. And one of my jobs was to install a shaved system into his chevelle he is building. I would LOVE to have that on the Fiero.||||reg||1
Z||000002||chester||09-25-2001||09:39 AM||||I'm giving my GT this treatment over the winter season.  Already have the electric release kit.  I'm going to wire it to my Alpine alarm remote so I can pop the doors open from a distance.  Should be pretty cool.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Will also keep the kids out of my car during shows.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> I plan on hiding some sort of a plug for jumper cables outside of the car just in case the old battery take a dive.<P><BR>Rob D.<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigline.jpg">   <BR>Modified 2.8<BR>2.5" Drop<BR>11" Brakes<BR>17" Revolutions<BR>RCC Coilover Suspension||||reg||14
